    "prompt": "Researchers administered a blend of natural antioxidants to aged mice and found that the animals navigated mazes faster and remembered previously learned routes. Muscle endurance was also improved. The authors see potential for preventing age-related memory loss in humans but warn that correct dosing is complex and excessive vitamin intake can be harmful. Clinical studies in humans are still pending.\n",
